      "text": "devil taketh him up into the holy city, Matt. 4:5. Give not that which is holy unto the dogs, Matt. 7:6 (3 Ne. 14:6). abomination of desolation … in the holy place, Matt. 24:15. come in his glory, and all the holy angels, Matt. 25:31. I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of God, Mark 1:24 (Luke 4:34). knowing that he was a just man and an holy, Mark 6:20. that holy thing which shall be born, Luke 1:35. spake by the mouth of his holy prophets, Luke 1:70. Every male … shall be called holy to the Lord, Luke 2:23. ye denied the Holy One and the Just, Acts 3:14. law is holy, and the commandment holy, Rom. 7:12. be holy, the lump is also holy: and if the root be holy, Rom. 11:16. living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, Rom. 12:1. temple of God is holy, which temple ye are, 1 Cor. 3:17. be holy and without blame, Eph. 1:4. framed together groweth unto an holy temple, Eph. 2:21. called us with an holy calling, 2 Tim. 1:9. thou hast known the holy scriptures, 2 Tim. 3:15. holy brethren, partakers of the heavenly, Heb. 3:1. as he … is holy, so be ye holy, 1 Pet. 1:15. built up a spiritual house, an holy priesthood, 1 Pet. 2:5. an holy nation, a peculiar people, 1 Pet. 2:9. holy men of God spake as they were moved, 2 Pet. 1:21. in all holy conversation and godliness, 2 Pet. 3:11. ye have an unction from the Holy One, 1 Jn. 2:20. holy city shall they tread under foot, Rev. 11:2. John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, Rev. 21:2.",
